module gunbc.rust_emitted_crate

import std.types { Bool, String }

// WHAT AN EMITTED RUST CLOSURE ASKS OF ITS CARGO WORKSPACE, AS A FACT THE EMISSION RETURNS. The
// emitter decides the crate name its main.rs paths through and the external crates its rendered
// code links; the crate partition (gunbc.emitted_crate_workspace) decides the layout those
// facts are realized in. Before this module the emitter rendered both into one Cargo.toml, so the
// single-package layout was baked into the emission; now the emission states what it needs and
// owns no manifest.
//
// This module lives under dag/ because the v1 emitter produces it and the host workspace writer
// reads it: one producer, several readers, no second list. It carries the facts only; the Cargo
// dependency rows the demand implies are rendered beside the manifests that list them
// (v1.compiler.stage0_crates emitted_crate_dependencies), so this module stays in the lowest
// partition crate with the emitted-edge facts it travels with.

// WHAT THE EMITTED CRATE DEPENDS ON IS DERIVED FROM WHAT WAS EMITTED, NOT DECLARED BESIDE IT. A
// fixed dependency list is a second authority for the crate's dependencies, free to disagree with
// the sources the same run just wrote, so the demand is a field the emission fills.
//
// THE RESIDUE IS NAMED RATHER THAN CLAIMED CLOSED. `ureq` sits in the base list on the same
// footing `clap` used to: it is referenced only when a corpus reaches the HTTP extdep, and nothing
// in the emitter's inputs says whether it did. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: an emission-level demand fact per
// external crate -- the renderer that emits a `ureq` call recording that it did -- at which point
// this carrier gains one field per dependency and the base list holds only what every emitted
// crate genuinely links.
type EmittedCrateDependencyDemand {
  renders_clap_cli: Bool
  renders_async_services: Bool
}

type EmittedRustCrate {
  crate_name: String
  demand: EmittedCrateDependencyDemand
}
